      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my 2018 civic is making this loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas. i think it might be a belt issue? can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a worn one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt, or drive belt, is a crucial component in your Civic's engine bay, acting like a very long, tough rubber band that connects the engine's power to various accessories. It's responsible for driving essential components like the alternator (which charges the battery), the power steering pump, and the water pump. When it's worn out, cracked, or slipping, it can start making that loud squealing noise you're hearing when you press the gas pedal.\n\nIt's a common issue, and it's a good idea to have a mechanic take a look at it soon before it causes a bigger problem. If the belt slips, you could lose power steering or even have your car overheat because the water pump stops working. You'll want to get it inspected promptly!",
